# "The owner of target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls shuffles it into their library."
#
# Turn 1: Bot1 casts Coveted Jewel (Black Lotus and three Moxen pay the {6}) and draws three. Turn 3: while Bot1 controls the
# Jewel it is not "an artifact an opponent controls", so Cathartic Parting cannot be cast (nothing else qualifies; the Elves is
# no artifact). Turn 4: Bot2's Llanowar Elves attacks unblocked, so Bot2 draws three and gains control of the Jewel. Turn 5: now
# the Jewel is an opponent's, Parting is cast on it and Bot1, its OWNER, shuffles it into Bot1's library - not Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Coveted Jewel
Cathartic Parting
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Coveted Jewel.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
! Bot1.Hand.Cathartic Parting.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cathartic Parting.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Coveted Jewel)
Bot1.Target()
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Library.Count = 9
Bot2.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Graveyard = Cathartic Parting; Black Lotus
